# Typing-Race environment
#
# Training needs NOTHING here: no server, no account, no network call. `pnpm install` then
# `pnpm dev` is the whole setup, and progress lives in the browser.
#
# Live races need a Supabase project. Copy this file to `.env.local` (never committed) and fill in
# the two values below; without them the "Races" page says calmly that races are unavailable and
# nothing else changes. Both values are public by design: the anon key is protected by row-level
# security, not by secrecy. Vite bakes them into the build, so set them before `pnpm build`.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL       Project URL, https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  The project's anon (public) API key
#
# Backend setup, once per project (Supabase CLI logged in, project linked with `supabase link`):
#   npx supabase db push              apply supabase/migrations
#   npx supabase config push          apply supabase/config.toml (enables anonymous sign-ins)
#   pnpm supabase:functions           bundle packages/* for Deno and deploy the Edge Functions
#
# The races e2e spec (`e2e/race.spec.ts`, tagged @backend) runs against this project and is
# skipped when these variables are absent.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
